-- title:
--   Level stalk at a crossing point: constants modulo non-units
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field and $A \subseteq L$ a valuation subring such that for all $a, b \in A$ with $a$ in the maximal ideal and $b \neq 0$ one has $b \mid a^{n}$ for some $n$. Let $X$ be an integral scheme with a proper, flat, locally of finite presentation morphism $\mathrm{toBase} : X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$. Let $A_0$ be a discrete valuation domain with uniformiser $\varpi_0$ generating its maximal ideal, and $\iota_0 : A_0 \to A$ an injective local homomorphism such that every element of $A$ is algebraic over the image of $\iota_0$; let $X_0$ be integral, proper, flat and locally of finite presentation over $\operatorname{Spec} A_0$, and let $\mathrm{iso}$ identify $X$ with $X_0 \times_{\operatorname{Spec} A_0} \operatorname{Spec} A$ compatibly with the structure morphisms to $\operatorname{Spec} A$. Let $x \in X$ lie over the closed point of $A$ and be closed (the only $y$ with $x \rightsquigarrow y$ is $x$), and let $x_0 \in X_0$ be its image. Assume $w \geq 1$ and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the $\mathfrak m$-adic completion of $\mathcal O_{X_0,x_0}$ onto the crossing model $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}(\mathrm{Fin}\,2, \hat A_0)/(X_0X_1 - C(\varpi_0^{w}))$, where $\hat A_0$ is the adic completion of $A_0$ and $\varpi_0$ is taken in $\hat A_0$, such that $e$ sends the image in the completion of the germ at $x_0$ of the global section of $X_0$ coming from $a \in A_0$ to the class of the constant series $C(a)$. Let further $A_1$ be a discrete valuation domain with uniformiser $\varpi_1$ generating its maximal ideal, $\iota_1' : A_0 \to A_1$ and $\iota_1 : A_1 \to A$ local homomorphisms with $\iota_1$ injective and $\iota_1 \circ \iota_1' = \iota_0$, and let $f_1 : X_1 \to \operatorname{Spec} A_1$, $g_1 : X_1 \to X_0$ form a pullback square over $\mathrm{toBase}_0$ and $\operatorname{Spec}(\iota_1')$, together with an isomorphism $e_1 : X \cong X_1 \times_{\operatorname{Spec} A_1} \operatorname{Spec} A$ compatible with the morphisms to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and such that the resulting map $X \to X_0$ through $X_1$ agrees with the one through $\mathrm{iso}$. Write $x_1$ for the image of $x$ in $X_1$. The conclusion is twofold: first, every $s \in \mathcal O_{X_1,x_1}$ admits $a \in A_1$ with $s$ minus the germ at $x_1$ of the global section of $X_1$ determined by $a$ a non-unit; second, the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O_{X_1,x_1}$ is contained in the sum of the image of the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O_{X_0,g_1(x_1)}$ under the stalk map of $g_1$ and the ideal generated by the germ at $x_1$ of the global section determined by $\varpi_1$.
--
--   This is the local analysis, at an intermediate discrete-valuation level $A_1$ between $A_0$ and the valuation ring $A$, of a proper flat integral model whose completed local ring at a closed special point is a crossing model $\hat A_0[[u,v]]/(uv - \varpi_0^{w})$: the level stalk is generated over the constants $A_1$ by non-units, and its maximal ideal is captured by the base-level maximal ideal together with the uniformiser $\varpi_1$. It feeds the normality statement [`AlgebraicGeometry.isIntegrallyClosed_stalk_pullback_of_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk_of_isDiscreteValuationRing`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.isIntegrallyClosed_stalk_pullback_of_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk_of_isDiscreteValuationRing) for stalks of the base-changed model.
